#X text 170 501 list:;
#X text 270 501 If the first element is a number \, it is considered
the message sending delay time in milliseconds. If this delay time
>0: it outputs the remaining elements of the list after this delay
time. If the delay time <0 \, it immediately outputs the remaining
elements of the list. If the delay time == 0 \, it outputs the remaining
elements of the list with the smallest possible delay (in the next
scheduler tick). If the first element is not a number \, immediately
output the entire(!) list.;
#X text 170 647 any:;
